## Cap map (facade truth)

| Facade | Token | Sealed op | Note |
|--------|-------|-----------|------|
| `process_spawn` / `wait` / `kill` | **ProcessCap** | `sys_spawn` / `sys_wait` / `sys_kill` | residual Err after seal |
| `process_exec` | **ProcessCap** | `sys_exec` | real fork+execvp+waitpid |
| `process_prctl` / epoll / inotify | **SysCap** | hard Sys residual | ProcessCap alone deny |
| `spawn_task` | **ProcessCap** | `async_spawn_internal` | SysCap supersede |
| `join_task` | **SysCap** | `async_join_internal` | hard residual |
| `load_model` | **SysCap** | `python_embed_internal` | **not** ProcessCap |

Legacy: `&SysCap` still supersedes ProcessCap preferred ops at check+runtime (one-wave compat).

